---
import { OPERATOR, PLAN_LINKS, SITE } from '../data/site';
interface Props { slug: string; plan?: { label: string; path: string }[] }
const links = PLAN_LINKS[Astro.props.slug] ?? (Astro.props.plan?.length ? Astro.props.plan : [{ label: 'Plan a stay in Portugal', path: '/plan-my-season' }]);
---
<aside class="plan" aria-labelledby="plan-h">
  <h2 id="plan-h">Plan this trip</h2>
  <p>When you are ready to book, go through a local operator rather than a stranger online. <a href={OPERATOR.url}>{OPERATOR.name}</a> is the Portugal operator listed in the <a href={SITE.directoryUrl}>Tourground directory</a>.</p>
  <p>{OPERATOR.summary}</p>
  {links.length > 0 && (
    <ul>
      {links.map((l) => <li><a class="pill" href={`${OPERATOR.url}${l.path}`}>{l.label} with {OPERATOR.name}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  )}
  <p>Before you pay anyone, ask for the company's registration number with Turismo de Portugal and a written confirmation of what you are paying for. Our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> explains how Navigator Coast and Tourground are connected.</p>
  <p class="fine">This box is not paid for and is not an endorsement or a review.</p>
</aside>
